<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mariano Ospina Rodríguez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1805">1805</a>–<a href="/years/1885">1885</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mariano Ospina Rodríguez was a Colombian politician, co-founder of the Conservative Party in 1849 and president from 1857 to 1861. The federal constitution of 1858, adopted under his government, created the Granadine Confederation. His attempts to strengthen central authority over the states led to the civil war in which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tomas-cipriano-de-mosquera">Tomás Cipriano de Mosquera</a> overthrew the government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mariano-ospina-rodriguez.jpg" alt="Mariano Ospina Rodríguez" width="221" height="300" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mariano_Ospina_Rodr%C3%ADguez.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
